    "result_text": "The full suite is green \u2014 `AcceptanceTest` is the only test class and both its tests pass.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the registration-date rule for `POST /api/owners`: when no `registrationDate` is supplied, it defaults to the server's current date, and the owner's `registrationDate` is returned in ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` format.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added an optional `registrationDate` field (`type: string, format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` schema, so it's bindable on create and returned in the `Owner` response. The generator produces a `LocalDate` property that Jackson serializes as `YYYY-MM-DD`.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** (entity) \u2014 Added a `LocalDate registrationDate` field mapped to a new `registration_date` column, with getter/setter and the `java.time.LocalDate` import.\n\n3. **`BuildOwner.java`** (the create pipeline's build step) \u2014 After mapping the request to the entity, defaults `registrationDate` to `LocalDate.now()` when the request didn't supply one. A supplied date is preserved (mapped by MapStruct by name).\n\n4. **`schema.sql`** for all four DBs (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres) \u2014 Added the `registration_date DATE` column to the `owners` table. Tests run on the hsqldb schema.\n\nThe MapStruct `OwnerMapper` maps `registrationDate` automatically by matching property name in both `OwnerFieldsDto \u2192 Owner` and `Owner \u2192 OwnerDto` directions, so no mapper change was needed.\n\n- `coreDefaultsToToday` \u2014 no date supplied \u2192 response `registrationDate` equals today \u2705\n- `functionalityKeepsSuppliedDate` \u2014 `2020-06-15` supplied \u2192 preserved and returned \u2705",
